  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="4eae-2172-16ff-c95e" name="Rise of Macedon (Alexander the Great) - List Notes" publicationId="0641-2ee1-c462-c414" hidden="false">
      <description>RISE OF MACEDON ARMY LIST 359-331 BC (Alexander the Great, pp.20-23). Percentages are by points. Characters up to 25%; the army must have a General (King Philip II, Alexander or a Strategos); any number of Hipparchs, Ilarchs or Taxiarchs up to the points limit. Cavalry up to 33%. Phalangites at least 25% (at least one phalanx unit). Skirmishers up to 25%. Special Troops, Mercenaries &amp; Allies up to 25%.
Oracles are used instead of Standards. War machines may not have leaders or musicians. Greek Mercenaries (Greek Mercenaries list; may be joined by Macedonian characters; Antipater up to 50%, Antigonos up to 50% plus 33% Persian levies by consent), Thracian allies (a Chieftain may command them as a Subordinate General; no Shamans) and Illyrian allies (0-1 Chieftain, 0-1 Light Cavalry, 0-1 Skirmishers) are documented only (no pick list); allied units never benefit from Oracles. Not enforced: Philip reduces the cavalry limit to 25%; one war machine per phalanx; one Agrianian unit per two other skirmisher units; mixed weapons in a unit; options that apply to all units alike.

ARMY COMPOSITION:
[Rise of Macedon]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Cavalry: up to 33%
  Phalangites: at least 25%
  Skirmishers: up to 25%
  Special Troops, Mercenaries &amp; Allies: up to 25%
  RISE OF MACEDON ARMY LIST 359-331 BC (Alexander the Great, pp.20-23). Percentages are by points. Characters up to 25%; the army must have a General (King Philip II, Alexander or a Strategos); any number of Hipparchs, Ilarchs or Taxiarchs up to the points limit. Cavalry up to 33%. Phalangites at least 25% (at least one phalanx unit). Skirmishers up to 25%. Special Troops, Mercenaries &amp; Allies up to 25%.
Oracles are used instead of Standards. War machines may not have leaders or musicians. Greek Mercenaries (Greek Mercenaries list; may be joined by Macedonian characters; Antipater up to 50%, Antigonos up to 50% plus 33% Persian levies by consent), Thracian allies (a Chieftain may command them as a Subordinate General; no Shamans) and Illyrian allies (0-1 Chieftain, 0-1 Light Cavalry, 0-1 Skirmishers) are documented only (no pick list); allied units never benefit from Oracles. Not enforced: Philip reduces the cavalry limit to 25%; one war machine per phalanx; one Agrianian unit per two other skirmisher units; mixed weapons in a unit; options that apply to all units alike.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
